WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:07.757
On a sunny

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:10.844
morning at Disney's Animal Kingdom

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:14.222
theme park,

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:17.684
the meerkats
come outside to catch some rays.

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:19.519
They like to lay in the sun.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.605
Some people call them solar powered,
so they sit like this

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:26.109
with their little bellies up to the sky.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:29.237
You'll see them kind of sitting
in the sun, taking it in, especially early

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:34.909
in the morning on those cooler mornings,
or if it's been kind of raining.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.245
There's so much
I love about working with the meerkats.

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:39.956
I try not to pick favorites.

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:43.043
I love all the meerkats very much,
and they all are very special.

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:45.545
Hi, buddy.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.338
You are so cute.

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:47.797
I know.

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:50.216
I love you.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.968
Can't favor you on camera.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:55.013
That's just embarrassing.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:58.224
These Southern African desert dudes

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.518
love their creepy crawly snacks.

00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:04.898
So today I'm feeding the meerkats,
super worms and mealworms.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:09.402
And they definitely love
those super worms is their favorite snack.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.863
I've been working with them
for a really long time.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.573
That means that I've been able to learn

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.825
all their individual quirks
and personalities,

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:18.953
and so I can sort of
tell them apart by what they're doing.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.207
Thomas Arlo.

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:25.210
Springsteen. Bentley

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.294
Nirvana.

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:29.881
Newt.

00:01:29.881 --> 00:01:35.345
At this moment in time, I would say that
Newton is probably our dominant animal.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:38.348
Which is surprising to me
because he's one of our youngest animals.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:43.186
Being the dominant male matters
in the meerkat market.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:47.190
Your job is kind of determined
in some ways by your social ranking

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:47.941
within the group.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:51.861
So in a typical group,
there would be a dominant female

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.406
who selects the dominant male
and they breed,

00:01:55.406 --> 00:01:59.953
and then the other members of the mob
are responsible for raising the offspring,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:04.541
finding food, taking sentry duty, which
means lookout to keep everybody safe.

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:08.128
All of that kind of stuff
falls on the other members of the group.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.004
Bentley’s in the back.

00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:14.175
They're scanning the sky
and the surrounding area to make sure

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:18.138
there are no threats that are imminent,
that everybody needs to be aware of.

00:02:20.223 --> 00:02:21.724
Bentley is a really fun guy.

00:02:21.724 --> 00:02:24.894
He is very chill.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:30.525
I would say he's really calm
and easygoing for the most part.

00:02:33.778 --> 00:02:36.197
Oh, so that was an alarm call.

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:40.326
Looks like he might have seen something
in the sky that I cannot see.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.080
They have a specific vocalization
for a sky

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:47.250
predator versus land predator.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.084
Something happened.

00:02:48.084 --> 00:02:51.546
We're all seeking shelter.

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:53.715
Oh. We're scared of the zebra.

00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:56.176
Those are our neighbors.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:59.262
You all know the zebra.

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:02.807
We're all underground.

00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:06.686
When the coast is clear, lower ranking

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:09.480
Bentley comes out with some attitude.

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:13.693
Bentley is definitely not in charge
and when it comes to our meerkat

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.736
social rankings.

00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:16.362
But sometimes he likes to try it out

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.199
and see how high he can get
and test the waters.

00:03:20.283 --> 00:03:24.787
But there's something brewing potentially.

